      "id": "patch_0517c5c2c927",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 5049,
      "mechanism": "Retain the previous cycle's input_axis_tready_reg value instead of forcing 0 in STATE_TRANSFER_OUT for EXPAND_BUS. This preserves the backpressure-driven ready signal that should be asserted when the output side can accept data (output_axis_tready_int_early=1), which is the root cause of cycle 8 input_axis_tready=0 vs expected 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_2a85c0d2ad99",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 6503,
      "mechanism": "Add output_axis_tready_int to the gate that sets input_axis_tready_next=0 on input_axis_tlast. When tlast arrives but the output is not ready (cycle 8), this prevents the FSM from latching input_axis_tready=0 and instead keeps it driven by output_axis_tready_int_early, fixing both input_axis_tready and the subsequent output_axis_tlast/tvalid mismatch at cycle 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_4f3a96077aa5",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 4599,
      "mechanism": "Qualify input_axis_tready_reg with !rst so the ready signal cannot be asserted during reset. This matches the protocol expectation that tready is only driven by valid backpressure after reset release, and prevents the early-cycle 0 that propagates into the cycle 8/9 failure window."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_7936cc858aae",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 8922,
      "mechanism": "Gate the STATE_IDLE input_axis_tready_next assignment with output_axis_tready_int so ready is only asserted when the output pipeline can actually accept a new word. This aligns the ready handshake with the output-side backpressure that is observed to be high at cycle 8."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_3cb99864f502",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 6503,
      "mechanism": "Require output_axis_tready_int alongside input_axis_tlast when clearing input_axis_tready_next. If the output is not ready (cycle 8), the ready signal stays asserted via output_axis_tready_int_early, preventing the spurious de-assertion that causes the cycle 8/9 mismatches."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_6c3f2cebb438",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 9435,
      "mechanism": "Add input_axis_tvalid to the STATE_TRANSFER_IN exit condition so the FSM only advances when a valid input word is present. This prevents a phantom transition that would otherwise drive input_axis_tready low and corrupt the output_axis_tlast/tvalid sequencing at cycle 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_e805e9a3d4c9",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 8922,
      "mechanism": "Invert the tlast qualification on the STATE_IDLE input_axis_tvalid gate so ready is asserted when tlast is low (normal streaming) rather than high. This keeps input_axis_tready asserted during the multi-cycle transfer that leads up to cycle 8, matching the observed backpressure."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_b689ecffefee",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 6503,
      "mechanism": "Require input_axis_tvalid when gating input_axis_tlast with output_axis_tready_int. This ensures the ready de-assertion only happens on a genuine last-word handshake, avoiding a false transition that would otherwise drop input_axis_tready at cycle 8 and corrupt cycle 9 outputs."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "The discovery trace shows three correlated failures at cycles 8–9: input_axis_tready stuck at 0 (expected 1), output_axis_tlast stuck at 0 (expected 1), and output_axis_tvalid stuck at 1 (expected 0). All eight candidates above target the FSM's ready/valid handshake logic around the EXPAND_BUS STATE_TRANSFER_OUT path and the STATE_IDLE entry gate. The top candidate (patch_0517c5c2c927) directly preserves the previous ready state instead of hard-coding 0, which is the minimal fix for the observed backpressure-driven ready assertion. The next four candidates (patch_2a85c0d2ad99, patch_4f3a96077aa5, patch_7936cc858aae, patch_3cb99864f502) add output_axis_tready_int or !rst qualifications to the same ready-assignment sites, ensuring the handshake respects output-side backpressure and reset. The remaining three (patch_6c3f2cebb438, patch_e805e9a3d4c9, patch_b689ecffefee) guard the STATE_TRANSFER_IN exit and STATE_IDLE entry with input_axis_tvalid/tlast qualifiers that prevent premature state transitions. Each citation points to the exact source line edited by the candidate and the failing port (input_axis_tready at cycle 8) that the edit addresses."
}
